NEW_SECTION
How to run, a section table, a "what it demonstrates" list, three consumer-side
techniques with the CSS for each, one caveat, and console notes.

REASON
Follows the structure CLAUDE.md asks for and that examples/autowriter/README.md
established. The "consumer-side techniques" section is the part that earns its place:
all three are things the library deliberately does not do, that a consumer will
otherwise hit and misread as the component being broken — a 2px handle that is hard
to grab and invisible at rest, a page stylesheet silently losing to resizer.css
because the module injects it later, and a left-handled box that resizes correctly
but appears to grow the wrong way because nothing anchored it.

The caveat records a real limitation rather than glossing it: handles are matched by
class name globally, so a style pushed through config.resizeHandlerProperties.styles
reaches every Resizer on the page. The workaround (a distinct class per instance via
config.myResizeHandler) is stated rather than left for the consumer to discover.
